{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f77e39d99b57bc5b72", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Chemical Kinetics - Test 3", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 37, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d923312f"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330ca", "title": "Chemistry Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233050", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b85"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b56"], "question": {"text": "Rate law for a reaction between A and B is given by<br />$\\mathrm{R}=\\mathrm{k}[\\mathrm{~A}]^{\\mathrm{n}}[\\mathrm{~B}]^{\\mathrm{m}}$<br />If concentration of A is doubled and concentration of $B$ is halved from their initial value, the ratio of new rate of reaction to the initial rate of reaction $\\left(\\frac{r_2}{r_1}\\right)$ is"}, "options": [{"id": "ef786a", "text": "$2^{(n-m)}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233051"}, {"id": "a46097", "text": "$(n-m)$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233052"}, {"id": "bed992", "text": "$(m+n)$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233053"}, {"id": "be554b", "text": "$\\frac{1}{2^{m+n}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233054"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233055", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "<p>For a first order reaction, the time required for completion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></math> reaction is &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>&#39; times the half life of the reaction. The value of &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>&#39; is</p><p>(Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3010</mn></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "1024cc", "text": "1.12", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233056"}, {"id": "4334bf", "text": "2.43", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233057"}, {"id": "280cfd", "text": "3.32", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233058"}, {"id": "252d7d", "text": "33.31", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233059"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923305a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b474c"], "question": {"text": "<p>Consider the given plots for a reaction obeying Arrhenius equation <math><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>:</mo></math> (<math> <mi>K</mi> </math>and <math><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></math> are rate constant and activetion energy, respectively )<br /><br />(I)&nbsp;<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fb67bb79e-7840-4e51-91c8-73f575d0d4e4-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 215px; height: 215px;\" /></p><p>(II)&nbsp;<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F0c91ad90-7d94-434c-900b-ac4eb1f7183c-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 203px; height: 212px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "5ac7c0", "text": "I is wrong but II is right", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923305b"}, {"id": "634e0a", "text": "Both I and II are wrong", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923305c"}, {"id": "940d5f", "text": "I is right but II is wrong", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923305d"}, {"id": "4d5ee4", "text": "Both I and II are correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923305e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923305f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478b"], "concepts": ["6162fbd06ed13040ec8535a8"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F4xR3Wy74WEdXd4FpGWx9L3qF84t5irCqTrjXhQ38UHc.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "4d730b", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233060"}, {"id": "bb346a", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233061"}, {"id": "15acb8", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233062"}, {"id": "be00ec", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233063"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233064", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "The rate of a certain biochemical reaction at physiological temperature <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> occurs <math><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></math> times faster with enzyme than without. The change in the activation energy upon adding enzyme is:"}, "options": [{"id": "a969e5", "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2.303</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233065"}, {"id": "b140a7", "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233066"}, {"id": "2d3c9c", "text": "<math><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2.303</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233067"}, {"id": "f126a0", "text": "<math><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233068"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233069", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e67"], "question": {"text": "The following results were obtained during kinetic studies of the reaction.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> product<br />&nbsp;<table border=\"1\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Experiment</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>in</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mol</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math> <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Initial rate of reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>in</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mol</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>min</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math><mn>6.93</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math><mn>6.93</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>30</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math><mn>1.386</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><br />The time (in minutes) required to consume half of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>A</mtext></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "819da1", "text": "<math><mn>100</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923306a"}, {"id": "25758a", "text": "<math><mn>10</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923306b"}, {"id": "596701", "text": "<math><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923306c"}, {"id": "a0ed6b", "text": "<math><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923306d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923306e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b85"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b56"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the following reaction; <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math></p><p><math><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>0.3010</mn></mrow></mrow></math></p><p>&lsquo;A&rsquo; and &lsquo;B&rsquo; respectively can be:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ca5bf8", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923306f"}, {"id": "ae5977", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233070"}, {"id": "9ed966", "text": "n-Butane and Iso-butane", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233071"}, {"id": "795bcb", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233072"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233073", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["6162fbd06ed13040ec85359f"], "question": {"text": "The reaction $2 \\mathrm{X} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{B}$ is a zeroth order reaction. If the\n\ninitial concentration of $\\mathrm{X}$ is $0.2 \\mathrm{M}$, the half-life is $6 \\mathrm{~h}$. When the initial concentration of $X$ is $0.5 \\mathrm{M}$, the time required to reach its final concentration of $0.2 \\mathrm{M}$ will be"}, "options": [{"id": "e94494", "text": "$9.0 \\mathrm{~h}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233074"}, {"id": "2b57a1", "text": "$12.0 \\mathrm{~h}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233075"}, {"id": "04e92c", "text": "$18.0 \\mathrm{~h}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233076"}, {"id": "614fe7", "text": "$7.2 \\mathrm{~h}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233077"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233078", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "<p>The rate constant&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></math> of a reaction is measured at different temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, and the data are plotted in the given figure. the activation energy of the reaction in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is gas constant)</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F5ce7d5e0-7ada-434d-9971-f94c7a9aa2f8-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 196px; height: 186px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "f39a55", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233079"}, {"id": "9ddd2e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923307a"}, {"id": "bbabe9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923307b"}, {"id": "45edb3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923307c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923307d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b85"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b56"], "question": {"text": "Consider an elementary reaction\n$\\mathrm{A}(\\mathrm{g})+\\mathrm{B}(\\mathrm{g}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C}(\\mathrm{g})+\\mathrm{D}(\\mathrm{g})$\nIf the volume of reaction mixture is suddenly reduced to $\\frac{1}{3}$ of its initial volume, the reaction rate will become ' $x$ ' times of the original reaction rate. The value of $x$ is :"}, "options": [{"id": "4deefb", "text": "$3$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923307e"}, {"id": "1563bc", "text": "$\\frac{1}{9}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923307f"}, {"id": "7bca5b", "text": "$9$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233080"}, {"id": "51134d", "text": "$\\frac{1}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233081"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233082", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "A flask contains a mixture of compounds <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>. Both compounds decompose by first-order kinetics. The half-lives for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, respectively. If the concentrations of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> are equal initially, the time required for the concentration of A to be four times that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;(in s) is : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>Use</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>693</mn><mo>)</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "4313bd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233083"}, {"id": "d9c01e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>900</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233084"}, {"id": "6df73d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233085"}, {"id": "ac58d3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233086"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233087", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "Consider the following statements related to temperature dependence of rate constants.<br />Identify the correct statements,<br />A. The Arrhenius equation holds true only for an elementary homogenous reaction.<br />B. The unit of A is same as that of k in Arrhenius equation.<br />C. At a given temperature, a low activation energy means a fast reaction.<br />D. A and Ea as used in Arrhenius equation depend on temperature.<br />E. When $\\mathrm{Ea} \\gg \\mathrm{RT}$. A and Ea become interdependent.<br />Choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "dee5fa", "text": "A, C and D Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233088"}, {"id": "24959b", "text": "B , D and E Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233089"}, {"id": "ee7271", "text": "B and C Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923308a"}, {"id": "f10bcd", "text": "A and B Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923308b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923308c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e67"], "question": {"text": "In a reaction $A+B \\rightarrow C$, initial concentrations of $A$ and $B$ are related as $[A]_0=8[B]_0$. The half lives of $A$ and $B$ are 10 min and 40 min. respectively. If they start to disappear at the same time, both following first order kinetics, after how much time will the concentration of both the reactants be same?"}, "options": [{"id": "a0f8a3", "text": "60 min", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923308d"}, {"id": "02fe86", "text": "80 min", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923308e"}, {"id": "54914c", "text": "20 min", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923308f"}, {"id": "1aa8f1", "text": "40 min", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233090"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233091", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "Consider the given plot of enthalpy of the following reaction between <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Identify the incorrect statement.<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F0cf951f8-f7fa-4899-a467-a7d410bfe384-image45.png?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "76806f", "text": "Formation of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> from <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> has highest enthalpy of activation.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233092"}, {"id": "23e233", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> is kinetically stable product.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233093"}, {"id": "d5afa0", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is the thermodynamically stable product.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233094"}, {"id": "420c22", "text": "Activation enthalpy to form <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is <math><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> less than that to form <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>.</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233095"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233096", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "In a first order decomposition reaction, the time taken for the decomposition of reactant to one fourth and one eighth of its initial concentration are $t_1$ and $t_2(s)$, respectively. The ratio $t_1 / t_2$ will :"}, "options": [{"id": "07192c", "text": "$\\frac{4}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233097"}, {"id": "37166e", "text": "$\\frac{3}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233098"}, {"id": "b00f85", "text": "$\\frac{3}{4}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d9233099"}, {"id": "d21b3d", "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923309a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923309b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "If a reaction follows the Arrhenius equation, the plot $\\ln k$\n\nvs $\\frac{1}{(\\mathrm{RT})}$ gives straight line with a gradient $(-\\mathrm{y})$ unit.\n\nThe energy required to activate the reactant is:"}, "options": [{"id": "30d243", "text": "$y / R$ unit", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923309c"}, {"id": "4c14d3", "text": "y unit", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923309d"}, {"id": "ca75f7", "text": "yR unit", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923309e"}, {"id": "68ce09", "text": "$-y$ unit", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d923309f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330a0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "For bacterial growth in a cell culture, growth law is very similar to the law of radioactive decay. Which of the following graphs is most suitable to represent bacterial colony growth ?\nWhere N - Number of Bacteria at any time, $\\mathrm{N}_0$ - Initial number of Bacteria."}, "options": [{"id": "215680", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FHOoxi2NzcT_4Ix7U6L8Omz5ThpW2ARgIB4TbPeTYsBI.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330a1"}, {"id": "291887", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FYjjfbxGr20EN1MnkjE7GSwzq4jqHW4hLluWg7J7HxqA.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330a2"}, {"id": "a00699", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F75UGyCe5DRoC0rSR0HPYqrhTi0O5az1SOmbeC0eOHB4.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330a3"}, {"id": "456dd0", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F2wDuvjLBmtTe6hQ3mYJLePhw8Yj-tvAXZ3hjT9b1WSk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330a4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330a5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "Reactant A converts to product D through the given mechanism (with the net evolution of heat) :<br />$\\mathrm{A} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{B} \\quad$ slow $; \\Delta \\mathrm{H}=+\\mathrm{ve}$<br />$\\mathrm{B} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C}$ fast; $\\Delta \\mathrm{H}=-\\mathrm{ve}$<br />$\\mathrm{C} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{D} \\quad$ fast ; $\\Delta \\mathrm{H}=-\\mathrm{ve}$<br />Which of the following represents the above reaction mechanism?"}, "options": [{"id": "f42750", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FzPx3Ur_ZdbLG6-lNQD7PYw_UQVx9CmF-sdYdC4MSlvw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330a6"}, {"id": "5c5d2f", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fg7LzJ88HpK4f-HnahPkWU1BuHeV5TU0wYR0O5qSSIBE.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330a7"}, {"id": "d5e8ff", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FJOSn6jXK_wO7GnuPyWJYy-gBdto3mMoUrXOkkCLxMDk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330a8"}, {"id": "a66d37", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F09vXzJMQj0ha3_MxKuiZYgrdIvjUirdsOH2tkwmMnAw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330a9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330aa", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "Which of the following statement is not true for radioactive decay?"}, "options": [{"id": "f2c024", "text": "Decay constant increases with increase in temperature.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330ab"}, {"id": "d8ef99", "text": "Amount of radioactive substance remained after three half lives is $\\frac{1}{8}$ th of original amount.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330ac"}, {"id": "735aaa", "text": "Decay constant does not depend upon temperature.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330ad"}, {"id": "e47747", "text": "Half life is $\\ln 2$ times of $\\frac{1}{\\text { rate constant }}$.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330ae"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330af", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "Consider the following plots of log of rate constant $\\mathrm{k}(\\log \\mathrm{k})$ vs $\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~T}}$ for three different reactions. The correct order of activation energies of these reactions is<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FyZnAFimwqdPE_Dqwif4lOJ9OGk7v2d7TJ6XsA-i_z50.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>"}, "options": [{"id": "bdaee3", "text": "$\\mathrm{Ea}_2 \\gt \\mathrm{Ea}_1 \\gt \\mathrm{Ea}_3$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330b0"}, {"id": "1bfc8f", "text": "$\\mathrm{Ea}_1 \\gt \\mathrm{Ea}_3 \\gt \\mathrm{Ea}_2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330b1"}, {"id": "7bb181", "text": "$\\mathrm{Ea}_1 \\gt \\mathrm{Ea}_2 \\gt \\mathrm{Ea}_3$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330b2"}, {"id": "8ca67a", "text": "$\\mathrm{Ea}_3 \\gt \\mathrm{Ea}_2 \\gt \\mathrm{Ea}_1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f112ee0e063d92330b3"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:33.957Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:33.957Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d923312d"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d923311c", "title": "Chemistry Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d92330fc", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9964"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f994a"], "question": {"text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> required for a reaction is produced by decomposition of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> as by equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>NO</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub></math><br/>The initial concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mol</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and it is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mol</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math> minutes.<br/>The rate of formation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi>mol</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>min</mi><mpadded voffset=\"-6px\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mpadded></math>, value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is ________."}, "options": [{"id": "82ec6c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d92330fd"}, {"id": "ecd3d8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d92330fe"}, {"id": "35c392", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d92330ff"}, {"id": "3f88fb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233100"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233101", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b85"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b56"], "question": {"text": "<p>For the decomposition of azomethane. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;a first order reaction, the variation in partial pressure with time at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is given as</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F7fc9241b-0f61-4342-9d09-778ad1b8816a-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 268px; height: 180px;\" /></p><p>The half life of the reaction is____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "c10ae2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233102"}, {"id": "15ddc1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233103"}, {"id": "92625c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233104"}, {"id": "f9842b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233105"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233106", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "$\\mathrm{A} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{~B}$\nThe molecule A changes into its isomeric form B by following a first order kinetics at a temperature of 1000 K . If the energy barrier with respect to reactant energy for such isomeric transformation is $191.48 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ and the frequency factor is $10^{20}$, the time required for $50 \\%$ molecules of A to become $B$ is _________ picoseconds (nearest integer). $\\left[\\mathrm{R}=8.314 \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\right]$"}, "options": [{"id": "497d99", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233107"}, {"id": "41d7c8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233108"}, {"id": "24d0eb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233109"}, {"id": "1fd6d3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d923310a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d923310b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "A sample of milk splits after <math><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> . at <math><mn>300</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> and after <math><mn>40</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> . at <math><mn>400</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> when the population of Iactobacillus acidophilus in it doubles. The activation energy (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math> ) for this process is closest to ______________.<br />(Given, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8.3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn></math> )"}, "options": [{"id": "37180f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d923310c"}, {"id": "f56851", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d923310d"}, {"id": "6f0aff", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d923310e"}, {"id": "79caab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d923310f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233110", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f46"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f1b"], "question": {"text": "A molecule undergoes two independent first order reactions whose respective half lives are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></math>. If both the reactions are occurring then the time taken for the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math> consumption of the reactant is ______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>min</mi></math>. (Nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "d4211c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233111"}, {"id": "71ff07", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233112"}, {"id": "8b0aaf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233113"}, {"id": "e0b455", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f122ee0e063d9233114"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:34.057Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:34.057Z", "__v": 0}, "pos